      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "To a stirred methanolic solution (25 mL) of H4L (0.040 g, 0.11 mmol), Gd(NO3)3·6H2O (0.075 g, 0.16 mmol) was added at room temperature, giving a clear yellow solution that was stirred for 10 minutes. Triethylamine (0.061 mL, 0.44 mmol) was then added dropwise, followed by 1,1,1-trifluoroacetylacetone (0.017 g, 0.11 mmol). The mixture was stirred for 5–6 hours at room temperature, filtered, and the volatiles were removed in vacuo. The yellow semi-solid residue was dissolved in methanol (5 mL) and diethyl ether was slowly diffused in; X-ray-quality crystals formed in 3–4 days.",
